WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:05.130
Rami is looking at an unfinished tower
in a fictional canal district.

2
00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:07.630
He’s thinking about buying
a flat off-plan.

3
00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:09.360
His question is simple.

4
00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:11.800
When buyers pay before
the building is finished,

5
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:13.341
where does that money go?

6
00:00:13.531 --> 00:00:15.831
A developer’s ordinary money pot

7
00:00:15.831 --> 00:00:18.962
and a project escrow account
are different ideas.

8
00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:21.042
In Dubai, the Land Department says

9
00:00:21.042 --> 00:00:24.402
an escrow account must be opened
in the name of the project,

10
00:00:24.402 --> 00:00:27.582
and used only for developing that project.

11
00:00:27.672 --> 00:00:32.052
Money received from off-plan buyers
goes into that project’s account,

12
00:00:32.052 --> 00:00:36.122
which is managed by an approved bank
or financial institution,

13
00:00:36.122 --> 00:00:37.880
called the account trustee.

14
00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:39.710
So how does money come out?

15
00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:43.900
The Land Department’s FAQ describes
major construction stages,

16
00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:45.800
set out in a written agreement.

17
00:00:45.890 --> 00:00:48.210
When the developer reports
a stage complete,

18
00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:52.500
the trustee’s engineer visits the site
to check it. After that check,

19
00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:56.373
the trustee can release payments
to the project’s service providers.

20
00:00:56.563 --> 00:00:58.893
Our miniature city is an analogy.

21
00:00:58.893 --> 00:01:00.680
It isn’t a real bank screen,

22
00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:04.033
or a promise that every contract
follows one schedule.

23
00:01:04.223 --> 00:01:08.303
Escrow is a control on where money goes
and how it’s released.

24
00:01:08.303 --> 00:01:11.173
It isn’t a promise that a building
finishes on time,

25
00:01:11.173 --> 00:01:13.003
that an investment makes money,

26
00:01:13.003 --> 00:01:15.133
or that a refund is automatic.

27
00:01:15.223 --> 00:01:17.413
Your own payments, and any dispute,

28
00:01:17.413 --> 00:01:20.846
depend on your actual contract
and the rules that apply.

29
00:01:21.036 --> 00:01:24.516
So before you rely on a brochure,
check three things.

30
00:01:24.516 --> 00:01:26.436
Match the exact project.

31
00:01:26.436 --> 00:01:29.626
Verify the official project
and account details.

32
00:01:29.626 --> 00:01:32.848
And check the project’s status
through official channels.

33
00:01:33.038 --> 00:01:36.208
A beautiful model shows
the building someone plans.

34
00:01:36.208 --> 00:01:38.675
The records show what you can verify.

35
00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:40.435
Ahmadreza Samadi.

36
00:01:40.435 --> 00:01:42.372
More at a-samadi.com
